193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 141 0 R
/E (Coral image classification presents significant challenges for traditional CNNs due to the dense, fine-grained visual patterns inherent to marine environments. While standard CNN architectures suffice when target coral species exhibit distinct, macro-level morphological features, fine-grained distinctions require a more robust approach. Consequently, this architecture serves as an effective foundation model for downstream fine-tuning.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
